# Node.js Architecture Guidelines

Structure for Node.js services. Australian English spelling throughout.

---

## Project Structure

Start flat for small services. When the service grows, separate by layer with dependencies pointing inward:

```text
src/
  domain/          # entities, value objects, domain errors — no framework imports
  application/     # use cases, port interfaces
  infrastructure/  # DB, queue, HTTP-client adapters implementing ports
  api/             # HTTP routes/handlers mapping requests to use cases
  config.ts        # typed, validated config (see node.mdc)
  main.ts          # composition root
```

For larger codebases, group by feature first (`src/orders/{domain,application,...}`).

---

## Layer Rules

- **Domain:** no external dependencies
- **Application:** depends on domain only; defines ports infrastructure must implement
- **Infrastructure:** implements ports; the only layer that imports DB drivers or SDKs
- **API / workers:** depend on application; translate transport ↔ use case
- Enforce boundaries with `eslint-plugin-boundaries` or `dependency-cruiser` once the codebase is large enough to drift

---

## Multiple Entry Points (Hexagonal)

HTTP servers, queue consumers, cron jobs, and CLIs are independent adapters calling the same use cases. The core never knows which adapter triggered it. Give each its own entry file (`main-http.ts`, `main-worker.ts`) sharing one composition function.

---

## Composition Root

- Wire from the outside in: load config → create infrastructure clients → construct use cases → start server/workers → register shutdown hooks
- Use plain constructor/function injection; a DI container is optional, not required
- Keep `main.ts` free of business logic
- Export a `buildApp(deps)` factory so tests can construct the app with fakes without listening on a port

---

## Module Boundaries

- One public entry per feature/module; avoid deep imports across features
- Avoid barrel `index.ts` re-exports of everything in large codebases — they slow type-checking and create cycles

---

## Checklist

- [ ] Dependencies point inward; domain/application import no infrastructure or framework code
- [ ] Each entry point is a thin adapter over shared use cases
- [ ] Composition root wires everything; `buildApp(deps)` testable without `listen()`
- [ ] No circular dependencies between features
